         {
          "h_title": "Breed Characteristics",
          "main_title": "\u200bCavapoo",
          "author": "The Lovely Pets",
          "language": "en",
          "level": 2,
          "primary_content": null,
          "secondary_content": [
           {
            "text": "Cavapoo is the very popular, designer crossbreed of a Cavalier King Charles spaniel and a miniature or toy poodle. They are extremely friendly to human, children and other pets alike. A Cavapoo is a terrific pup for first-time dog owners, families in search of an adorable playmate for children, or seniors who want an endearing companion.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
           },
           {
            "text": "In addition, their fur is often hypoallergenic due to its poodle parent. While the Mayo Clinic stresses that no dog is allergen-free, some people might have less reaction to the proteins found in a Cavapoo\u2019s dander, saliva, and urine.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
           },
           {
            "text": "As Cavapoo are a cross breed, their fur can range from short smooth fur (like a cavalier king charles) to a wavy silky fur or a curly poodle coat. The latter two are especially popular due to their non shedding property.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
           },
           {
            "text": "They are a medium size breed, typically weighing between 7-10kg, not too small and not too big! Their fur colour ranges from cream, to red, to brown to black which comes with or without markings.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
           },
           {
            "text": "Cavapoos are very similar in looks and temperament to Cockapoos, with cockapoos as the slightly larger cousin.",
            "url": null,
            "urls": null
           }
          ],
          "table_content": null
         },
